{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/concepts/work-loop.md at f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12 on request/commitment-honesty. Successor to the artifact naming f6244ac5.\n\nThe page describes the commitment lifecycle, and this branch moved it: ten statuses instead of eight, satisfaction terminal, and a retirement by anyone other than the author reading revoked for a request and released for a promise. It now rests on the fold that produces those statuses and on the lane classification that decides which of them a reader is shown.\n\nIts previous anchor was retired. That is worse than out of date: a retired artifact is a pointer somebody withdrew, so the page had already flared and nobody re-anchored it, and the flare did its job and was ignored. Ten pages across the set are in that position, measured and recorded against request 3842d0a9.\n\nThe prose corrections this head carries are as important as the anchoring. The page said the fold projects eight statuses when it projects ten — my earlier edit to that line was a silent no-op and I reported it fixed anyway. And it said a released commitment wants a new performer, which is wrong: the request stays addressed to the same signed actor and can take a replacement promise from them, unless the request itself is replaced.","body":{"branch":"request/commitment-honesty","commit":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","head":"f83d5cd52d7588abc78d716c157d53056cd36d12","path":"docs/concepts/work-loop.md"}}